@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; Axiom 7 folding .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm: the cubic has three real
; common tangents and every one of them cuts the sheet, so the paper filter
; keeps all three. Each lands .a or .c beside the paper of its line, so no
; fold carries out both alignments (ADR 0031).

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --vm             ; vertical midline x = 1/2
--x = (map .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm)

; expect error "no fold of map .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm carries out all its alignments at once"
